    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60670" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύκν-ειος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			LXX
			<u>4 Ma.</u>
			15.21
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of a
			swan</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτίλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					1127.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στόμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.12
				</span></i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ κ.</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆσμα</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλος</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ᾄδειν</span>
			<i>a swan's dying song</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				3.199
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				2.32
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. πρὸς φιληκοΐαν φωναί</span>
			LXXl.c.: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ κ. ἐξηχεῖν,
			ἐξᾷσαι</span>, to make a last appeal, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				30.4.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				31.12.1
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				31.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύκνειος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i>of
				Cycnus</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					10(11).15
				</span></i>
			.</div>
